    {
      "claim_id": "C371_GAUGE",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX371_BRIDGE",
        "content_hash": "9ac30de5c4dbe55e664b5ec968cc8ce408b8c454d98492fde79f886b8613bd42"
      },
      "natural_statement": "The substitution q_h=r^(11/2) exp(hi r^2/8) v_h produces F_h=r^2/16+b-h omega-L_ell/r^2 and imaginary term hi(sigma+a-3), with the corresponding exact matrix-coupling phases and simple-turn scales.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "9965f6728481c29d203869044401fd267f88824eea15ccaf6578b19b9df40df1"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C371_REMOTE",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX371_BRIDGE",
        "content_hash": "9ac30de5c4dbe55e664b5ec968cc8ce408b8c454d98492fde79f886b8613bd42"
      },
      "natural_statement": "Under the stated exterior Euler-symbol hypotheses, every symbol-outgoing solution has q'_h(E)-hi sqrt(F_h(E))q_h(E)=O(E^-1)|q(E)| uniformly along either escaping regime, E=16 sqrt(max(1+ell,omega)).",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "b8496a9d981e6c4723fbc3bb7e519b884ca7107eba7359dbbae3849f5a80c90a"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C371_SCALAR",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX371_BRIDGE",
        "content_hash": "9ac30de5c4dbe55e664b5ec968cc8ce408b8c454d98492fde79f886b8613bd42"
      },
      "natural_statement": "For F_h=r^2/16+b-h omega-L_ell/r^2 and bounded real gamma, scalar transfer and a nonvanishing normalized growing-branch coefficient imply U'_h(R)/U_h(R)=B_h(R)+o(n_*), uniformly on the fixed shell in both escaping regimes.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "931d151eb49b14a70ee5b1b1f7ecb40ffbd93ecd907899741919dd0b252d92e6"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C371_COUPLED",
      "version": 1,
      "context": {
        "kind": "context",
        "subject_id": "CTX371_BRIDGE",
        "content_hash": "9ac30de5c4dbe55e664b5ec968cc8ce408b8c454d98492fde79f886b8613bd42"
      },
      "natural_statement": "Given uniform scalar transfer and endpoint value margins, the mixed Dirichlet/outgoing Green operator for arbitrary bounded r^-2 matrix coupling is small in the joint K-weighted norm; the two channel actions need not be compared.",
      "formal_statement": "",
      "external_assumptions": [],
      "retired_assumptions": [],
      "content_hash": "a056f9490245894e6486f9110ba2df9778c37a266da6d7852a613af19e90ca0f"
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "C371_SHELL",
      "version": 1,
