        "subject_id": "CTX371_BRIDGE",
        "content_hash": "9ac30de5c4dbe55e664b5ec968cc8ce408b8c454d98492fde79f886b8613bd42"
      },
      "natural_statement": "For the circular spectral system under the explicit bounded-parameter and exterior symbol hypotheses, the outgoing-to-fixed-shell map is a graph q'=diag(B_h)q+o(n_*)q in operator norm in both escaping regimes, including turning-point passage and channel coupling.",
